course: dictionary
lesson: 12112
title: Collected: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Collected is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Mum collected the eggs from the hen house.» Here collected means gathered together, picked up from one place. «Sam has collected stamps since he was six.» Here collected means kept as a hobby. «When the fire alarm rang, Mrs Lee stayed calm and collected.» Here collected means calm and in control.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. Collected is the past of collect, so it tells you that something has already happened.
fact: Collected is the past of collect, which means to gather things together.
fact: «Collected» can describe stamps, coins or cards that someone keeps as a hobby.
fact: «Collected» can also describe a person who stays calm and in control.
fact: In maths, «collected» can mean things gathered and added up, as in «the sweets collected in all».
fact: In science, data is what scientists collect: the facts and numbers they gather in an experiment or survey.
exercise: «Mum collected the apples from under the tree.» What does collected mean here? | Lost | *Gathered together | Kept as a hobby | Calm and in control
exercise: «Amir has collected football cards for three years.» What does collected mean here? | *Kept as a hobby | Gathered together in one pile | Thrown away | Calm and in control
exercise: «The scientists collected data from forty plants.» What did the scientists collect? | Calm feelings | Stamps | *Facts and numbers | Old coins
test: «Even in the storm, the captain stayed calm and collected.» What does collected mean? | Scattered | *Calm and in control | Kept as a hobby | Gathered together
test: In maths, «the sweets collected in all came to thirty-six». What does collected mean here? | Calm and in control | *Gathered and added together | Kept as a hobby | Lost
exam: «The lost dog was collected from the park by its owner.» What does collected mean here? | Calm and in control | *Gathered and taken away | Kept as a hobby | Counted by the teacher
